  "body": "Closes #824\nClaim: mac/mac-mbp\nAuthor model: Sonnet 5.5 (mac/mac-mbp-w824)\n\n### Problem\nOperator decision 2026-11-28 (#824): the Favoris tab and screen are titled « Favoris », as legacy, never « Drapeaux » (GAP-032). The title bar and the tab item already say « Favoris » (`TopicSource.navigationTitle`, #975); the one place left was the list picker of the tab's menu, which still offered « Favoris » and « Drapeaux ».\n\n### Cause\n`TopicSource.title` (the picker entry) named the flags list « Drapeaux » and the favourites list « Favoris », while legacy names its two modes « Drapeaux & Favoris » and « Favoris uniquement » (`AppSettingsView.swift:129-132` @ 87fe0d1c), as Réglages already does.\n\n### Change\n`TopicSource.title`: `.flagged` is « Drapeaux & Favoris », `.favorites` is « Favoris uniquement ». Nothing else renamed: the flags concept keeps « drapeaux » where it means the flags (sign-in prompt, success sentences, doc comments).\n\n### Tests\n`TopicSourceTitleTests/favorisTabTitle()` pins both navigation titles and both picker names (red before the change, green after; iOS 27.2 simulator, 1 test run and passed).\nSwiftLint rules checked by hand on the two touched files: line_length (140), file_length, type_body_length, vertical_whitespace.\n\n### Ledger\n\n```gap-edit\nGAP-032\nSwiftHFR final: The Favoris tab and screen are titled « Favoris » as legacy (operator, 2026-11-28, #824); the list picker names the two modes as legacy, « Drapeaux & Favoris » and « Favoris uniquement ».\n```\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_014QH2CEAZJkg4akNJrTQb2i\n",
