   "body": "**Adversarial review (Opus 5.5, mac/mac-mbp-r1447, head d2b89eeb)**: APPROVE\n\nThe PR does what it claims. `TopicSource.title` has one consumer, the \"Liste\" picker of `FavoritesSourceMenu` (`RootTabsView.swift:130`), which appears on both the iPhone tab and the iPad sidebar (`RootSidebarView.swift:118`). Choosing an entry writes the favourites mode (`NavigationModel.swift:18`), so taking the Réglages names (`SettingsView.swift:83-84`) is the right fix: one setting, one pair of names. The title bar and the tab item already say « Favoris » (`navigationTitle`, `RootTab.swift:30`). The app has no widgets, intents, shortcut items or VoiceOver label that use these strings. Where « drapeaux » still appears, it means the flags (the sign-in line, doc comments).\n\nFindings (none blocking):\n\n1. **Low**: `RootModel.swift:380` (`favoritesSources = [.favorites, .flagged]`), which this PR does not change. The menu now shows « Favoris uniquement » before « Drapeaux & Favoris ». Legacy (`AppSettingsView.swift:129-132` @ 87fe0d1c) and Réglages show the same two names in the other order. A user who sees the same pair in two orders may think they are different settings. Fix: `[.flagged, .favorites]`, or say on the PR why the order differs.\n2. **Detail**: `TopicSource.swift:22-23`. The `navigationTitle` doc comment still says \"`title` stays the list's own name\". After this PR, `title` is the mode name. Fix: \"the favourites mode's name\".\n3. **Detail**: the PR body says `Closes #824`, but #824 is already closed (\"nothing is left\", cloud/orch). Use `Refs #824`, or say that the issue was reopened, so the close-after-merge step does not look skipped.\n\nThe legacy citation is correct: `87fe0d1c:HFRswift/Swift/AppSettingsView.swift:130-131` holds both strings, and lines 129-132 are the whole array. The `gap-edit` is valid and accurate. GAP-037 (also in #824's scope) is already done in #1316/#1317.\n\n**Verified**: worktree at d2b89eeb (merge base e672de7c = dev-swift); read the diff and every consumer of `TopicSource.title` and every « Drapeaux » / « Favoris » string under `App/SwiftHFR`; `git grep` at 87fe0d1c for the legacy strings; `python3 tooling/docs/ledger.py check-body` (1 block ok); checked the GAP-032 header and row; checked that no touched line is over 140 characters; CI SwiftLint, Docs consistency and Pre-commit green (the 2 s app-build failure is the draft gate). Not run: the app test on a simulator. I checked statically that the new expectations fail on the old strings.\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code)_\n",
